      "body": "- `nvim --version`: `NVIM v0.5.0-dev+1423-ge2d3ad7bc`\r\n- Operating system/version: Ubuntu 21.04\r\n- Terminal name/version: Knosole 20.12.3\r\n- `$TERM`: xterm-256color\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nRun `python3 scripts/gen_vimdoc.py --target api` to generate documentation.\r\n\r\n### Actual behaviour\r\n\r\nThe documentation for `zindex` under `nvim_open_win` (`:help nvim_open_win()`) is not wrapped properly, and spaces are omitted surrounding the word `zindex`, between `higher` and `go`. The data used to generate the documentation, from `nvim/api/vim.c`, appears fine.\r\n\r\n![zindex](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/541289/123374057-7dd4cf80-d554-11eb-87c0-78482c15b3fa.png)\r\n\r\n### Expected behaviour\r\n\r\nProper wrapping and spaces retained.\r\n\r\n### Additional information\r\n\r\nRemoving the following lines in `nvim/api/vim.c` results in the proper output from `gen_vimdoc.py` for the text that precedes those lines.\r\n\r\n```\r\n///       - 100: insert completion popupmenu\r\n///       - 200: message scrollback\r\n///       - 250: cmdline completion popupmenu (when wildoptions+=pum)\r\n```",
